# 2026-11-18 evening: restricted file-read APIs and further WP PHP enumeration
# The supplied Telegram text displays "&amp;" in two query strings; verify
# raw Nginx escaping before considering a promotion to active Fail2Ban regexes.
api-system-fileview-env|REVIEW|api-file-read-secret|/api/system/fileView\?file=/app/\.env(?:$|&)|API file-view targeting an env file; verify actual route and Nginx escaping
api-fs-outside-workspace-env|REVIEW|api-file-read-secret|/api/fs/read\?allowOutsideWorkspace=true(?:&|&amp;)path=/app/\.env(?:$|&)|Attempts reading env outside workspace; not a generic /api/fs/read ban
api-console-traversal-env|REVIEW|api-query-traversal|/api/console/api_server\?sense_version=%40%40SENSE_VERSION(?:&|&amp;)apis=(?:\.\./){3,}\.env(?:$|&)|Query-based env traversal; check whether pasted &amp; is display escaped
adjacent-dotenv-media|REVIEW|path-traversal-variant|/media\.\./\.env(?:$|\?)|Adjacent-dot path; not necessarily traversal unless server routing is vulnerable
php-configuration-backup|REVIEW|php-config-backup|/configuration\.php\.bak(?:$|\?)|Potential sensitive backup, review in context
wordpress-optimizer-php|REVIEW|wordpress-suspicious-php|/wp-optimizer\.php(?:$|\?)|Unconfirmed PHP probe; correlate with recurring Azure batches
wordpress-login-lookalike-capital-i|REVIEW|wordpress-obfuscated-login|/wp-Iogin\.php(?:$|\?)|Capital I rather than lowercase l in login; preserve case for evidence
wordpress-config-query|REVIEW|php-config-probe|/config\.php\?(?:$|[^ ]*)|Observed trailing question mark; may be legitimate, never one-hit ban

# 2026-11-19: combined config, secret and SQL backup enumeration (same IP/second)
secrets-json-yaml|REVIEW|secret-file-discovery|/secrets\.(?:json|ya?ml)(?:$|\?)|Sensitive-looking file, but require corroboration before active one-hit ban
env-frontend-js|REVIEW|frontend-env-discovery|/env\.js(?:$|\?)|May be a deliberately public frontend configuration file; avoid one-hit bans
env-frontend-double-underscore|REVIEW|frontend-env-discovery|/__ENV\.js(?:$|\?)|May be deliberately public runtime configuration; case-sensitive review

